> > Because the way that the game calculates "how much damage do I need to
> > inflict here to be automatically fatal?" is to double max HP and add
> > 200; the doubling is to allow for half physical damage, the 200 for
> > AC. It used to just inflict fixed large numbers, but people were
> > evading that.
> 
> Umm, scratching head, why doesn't it just inflict "MAXINT or whatever" 
> (possibly add or substract AC depending on where in code it is).

Because it's calculating a damage bonus (to be added to the artifact's
usual weapon damage), not final damage; you don't want final weapon
damage to wrap. Adding "MAXINT - (some amount)" would work but become
survivable by half physical damage at just about the same point, so
doesn't gain you much. (Well, you'd be doing huge-amount of damage
rather than 0, which is somewhat more reasonable, but I don't think
there's much mileage in arguing edge cases.)

